WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.050
Star Wars: The Force Awakens...is like the
world's geekiest Easter egg hunt. J.J.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:14.150
Abrams told audiences to pay close
attention to their movie screens and

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.770
they'll be filled with delicious
references from Star Wars' past. However

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:21.570
this seemed to be harder than expected,
there were so many hidden treasures, we had to

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:26.359
watch the film a few times to get it all. I mean, not that we mind, I saw it like three times already but (clears throat)

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.220
NUMBER ONE: FN 2187

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.780
Before donning the name Finn,
stormtrooper FN 2187 shared the same

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:38.149
number as the cell block on the Death Star that held Princess Leia. He also shares that

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:41.690
number with an abstract short film that
influenced George Lucas. Both of these

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:45.430
reasons probably led to Finn's allegiance
changing. That and all of the other

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:50.030
stormtroopers used to laugh and call him
names. They never let poor FN 2187 join in any

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:51.110
stormtrooper games.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:55.500
NUMBER TWO:  YODA AND OBI-WAN ARE IN THE FORCE AWAKENS

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:02.180
When Ray touches Luke's lightsaber, wow that sounds dirty, she starts having visions and hears voices. J.J. Abrams

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:06.380
confirmed that if you listen hard enough,
you can hear Luke, Obi-Wan, and Yoda.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:11.620
A young and old Obi-Wan delivers the
line "Rey, this is your first step."

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:15.720
Alec Guinness, who played Obi-Wan in the
original trilogy, passed away in 2000, but

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.710
was able to reprise the role post-mortem
do some clever editing. By truncating

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:24.549
audio of Guinness saying the word "afraid," Abrams had an older Obi-Wan say "Rey," and

00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:28.300
asked Ewan Mcgregor to reprise his role
as the younger Obi-Wan to complete the line.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.480
NUMBER THREE: SECRET CAMEOS

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.740
There's a few casting surprises that you may have missed. The stormtrooper watching over the captive Rey

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.520
who falls for the old Jedi mind trick was played by
Daniel Craig. He was at Pinewood Studios

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.820
filming Spectre and did the cameo for S's and G's.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:47.220
Carrie Fisher's daughter Billie Lord plays a lieutenant in the Resistance. There are some

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.340
interesting music connections in the
film too. Radiohead producer Nigel Godrich

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:57.600
and composer Michael Giacchino play
stormtroopers FN 9330 and FN 3181, which

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:02.200
is also a reference to George Lucas' film
THX 1138. One of the alien Resistance

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.649
pilots is named Ello Asty after the Beastie Boys album Hello Nasty. He also has "Born To Ill"

00:02:06.649 --> 00:02:10.580
on his helmet. Even writer-director and
super Star Wars fan Kevin Smith has a

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:11.940
cameo as a stormtrooper.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.800
And no he wasn't silent.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.360
NUMBER FOUR: MAZ KANATA'S SECRETS

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:20.780
Some of the flags outside of Maz Kanata's castle include some of the same flags from the Boonta Eve

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:25.000
podrace, as well as a Mandalorian flag, the same symbol featured on Boba Fett's armor.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:29.650
Also, could the chest Maz Kanata keeps Luke's lightsaber in be the same chest that

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:34.410
Obi-Wan keeps in a New Hope? Who knows, only time and sequels will tell.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:37.270
NUMBER FIVE: RALPH MCQUARRIE'S INSPIRATIONS

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:41.400
In 1975, George Lucas hired concept artist Ralph McQuarrie

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:45.970
to create tons of concept art in order
to get financing for Star Wars. Abrams has

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:49.750
used some of these pieces of art as
inspiration for his Star Wars movie. At

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:53.080
one point, George Lucas was going to have
the main character be a woman, and have

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:56.840
McQuarrie create some possible looks for her. Rey's costume may have been inspired by

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.390
concept art from that session. The arch in Niima outpost is from McQuarrie's

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:04.190
sketches of Jabba's palace, and BB-8 was
inspired from one of McQuarrie's concept

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:08.030
art for R2D2. Funnily enough, the character of Zeb Orrelios from Star Wars

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:11.320
Rebels is also inspired by original
concept art for Chewbacca.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.540
NUMBER SIX: "THIS IS A RESCUE"

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:17.120
In the beginning, Finn rescues Poe from the Finalizer. As

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.460
they're about to escape, Finn takes off
his helmet and says "this is a rescue!"

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:25.660
That little piece of dialogue is a major throwback. Remember when Luke meets Leia for the first time in the

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:31.020
original Star Wars? Luke takes off his stormtrooper mask and says "I'm Luke Skywalker, I'm here to rescue you!"

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.680
Now Finn might not be the next Luke in the series, but it was still a great reference.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:38.720
Han Solo also blurts out another familiar
line from the franchise: "I've got a bad feeling

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.569
about this," which is heard in every Star
Wars film.

00:03:41.569 --> 00:03:43.149
Great job on that addition J.J.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:45.960
NUMBER SEVEN: MORE FUZZY PARSEC MATH

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:50.959
Another famous line in the original Star Wars is when Han Solo boasts that the Millennium Falcon made the

00:03:50.959 --> 00:03:55.299
Kessel run in less than 12 parsecs. The
nerdiest fans love and hate this line

00:03:55.299 --> 00:03:59.700
because a parsec is a unit of measurement, not time. However, we hear that simple mistake

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:03.530
used again when Rey and Han are talking about how many parsecs it took to make the

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:07.030
Kessel run when the two meet on the
Falcon. Both characters don't seem to be

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.670
phased by their mathematical mistake.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:10.830
NUMBER EIGHT: THE WILHELM SCREAM

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:15.300
The Wilhelm Scream was first recorded in 1951 and made famous in the movie The Charge At

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:18.900
Feather River by Private Willhelm. Private Wilhelm's scream might just be the

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:24.260
most famous scream in movie history.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:28.720
It has been every single Star Wars film, as
well as about 200 other movies. During

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:32.120
Finn and Poe's escape from the First Order hangar bay, an unlucky stormtrooper belts

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:36.860
out a recognizable sound. Keep your ears sharp next time you see the scene, you'll hear Private Wilhelm.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:39.360
NUMBER NINE: FINN FINDS SOME OLD TOYS

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:41.260
While Finn is rifling through stuff to help

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:46.070
heal Chewbacca's wounds on the Millennium Falcon, he finds a well-known
object. As Luke was training on the

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:50.400
Falcon, he used the help of a flying remote. Finn finds that remote but then quickly

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.190
tosses it aside as he keeps searching
for medical supplies. Later, Finn bumps

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:58.770
into a chessboard and turns on a holochess game. A Marksman-H Combat Remote and holochess

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.970
in one scene? We can feel the fan jaws
dropping.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.080
NUMBER TEN: GET LOST

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:08.020
Okay this one may not have to do with Star Wars, but has more to do with J.J. Abrams.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:12.300
Two actors who are well known for working with the director have major cameos in this film.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:16.680
Greg Grunberg suited up as an X-Wing pilot named Snap Wexley. Another actor from

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:21.170
the Lost series, Ken Leung, also pops up here as Admiral Statura. Being friends with J.J.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.970
means you get cameos in his film. Best friendship ever.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:27.520
And finally NUMBER ELEVEN: THE STARKILLER BASE

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.580
The First Order took a page
from the Empire's playbook and also

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:34.410
gives us one of the biggest Easter eggs
in all of The Force Awakens. The film's

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.600
villains built themselves a gigantic
super weapon capable of destroying

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:42.370
entire systems, suns and all. Instead of
calling it the Death Star, they call the

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:46.030
weapon the Starkiller base. You're
probably asking yourself why this deadly

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.480
object is so important.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.420
Well, its name was the original surname
George Lucas intended to give Luke. Yes

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:53.050
our favorite Jedi was almost

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:57.470
Luke Starkiller. Good thing he went with Skywalker, Starkiller is definitely a better name for a planet

00:05:57.470 --> 00:06:01.010
destroying device. The Force Awakens stands to be one of the greatest in the Star Wars

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:05.470
series. What made it so great was that J.J. was a creative fan. After seeing

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:09.240
this video, we hope it inspires you to re-watch the newest addition to the series.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:12.200
Use the force and find those Easter
eggs!

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:29.330
Thanks for watching, and don't forget to
like and subscribe if you want to see

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:30.289
more. See you next time!

